{"Name": "document3", "Natural": "Here is a summarized version of the text, keeping only the most important information:\n\n**Young Sheldon**\n\n* American television sitcom (2017-2024)\n* Prequel to The Big Bang Theory\n* Developed by Chuck Lorre and Steven Molaro\n* Premiered on CBS on November 2, 2017\n\n**Cast**\n\n* Iain Armitage as Sheldon Cooper\n* Zoe Perry as Mary Cooper\n* Lance Barber as George Cooper Sr.\n* Montana Jordan as George Cooper Jr.\n* Raegan Revord as Melissa \"Missy\" Cooper\n* Annie Potts as Constance \"Meemaw\" Tucker\n\n**Synopsis**\n\n* The series follows Sheldon Cooper's early life as a child prodigy in Medford, Texas\n* It explores his relationships with his family and friends, and his struggles to fit in\n\n**Reception**\n\n* Critical acclaim, with a 76% approval rating on Rotten Tomatoes\n* Metacritic score of 63 out of 100\n* Won several awards, including the ReFrame Stamp for gender-balanced hiring\n\n**Spin-off series**\n\n* Georgie & Mandy's First Marriage, a spin-off series focusing on Georgie Cooper and Mandy McAllister, is in development\n*"}
{"Name": "document2", "Natural": "Here is a summary of the text in 2-3 sentences:\n\nYoung Sheldon season 7 will premiere on E4 on July 21st at 8pm, following the finale's US release earlier this year. The final season will continue to follow Sheldon Cooper's story, with the cast including Iain Armitage, Zoe Perry, and others. The plot will address \"larger events\" that have shaped Sheldon's life, but details are being kept under wraps to avoid spoiling the series."}
{"Name": "document4", "Natural": "Here is a summary of the text in 2-3 sentences:\n\nThe TV series \"Young Sheldon\" is a spin-off of \"The Big Bang Theory\" and follows the life of Sheldon Cooper as a child. The show explores Sheldon's childhood in Texas, his relationships with his family and friends, and his struggles with social interactions and his exceptional intelligence. The series premiered in 2017 and has since aired seven seasons, with the final season concluding in 2024."}
{"Name": "document10", "Natural": "Here is a summary of the text in 2-3 sentences:\n\nLake Mead is the largest manmade lake in the US, with a capacity of 28.76 million acre-feet at full pool. It was created by the Hoover Dam on the Colorado River and supplies water to over 25 million people in Nevada, Arizona, California, and Mexico. The lake faces challenges from drought and urbanization, but conservation measures and innovative solutions are being implemented to ensure its survival."}
{"Name": "document7", "Natural": "Here is a summary of the text in 2-3 sentences:\n\nThe top 5 largest man-made lakes in the United States are Lake Mead, Lake Powell, Lake Sakakawea, Lake Oahe, and Fort Peck Lake, ranked by volume. Lake Mead, located on the Arizona-Nevada border, is the largest with a capacity of 28.76 million acre-feet, followed by Lake Powell with a capacity of 26 million acre-feet."}
{"Name": "document6", "Natural": "Here is a summary of the text in 2-3 sentences:\n\nThe 10 largest reservoirs in the United States are listed, including Lake Francis Case, Toledo Bend Lake, Lake Shasta, Lake Koocanusa, Franklin D. Roosevelt Reservoir, Fort Peck Lake, Lake Sakakawea, Lake Oahe, Lake Powell, and Lake Mead. These reservoirs provide water supply, hydroelectric power, recreation, and wildlife habitat, and are operated by various government agencies and organizations. The largest reservoir, Lake Mead, is located on the Colorado River and has a total capacity of 28,255,000 acre-feet."}
{"Name": "document8", "Natural": "Here is a summary of the text in 2-3 sentences:\n\nThe top 10 largest man-made lakes in the world are listed, with Lake Volta in Ghana being the largest. These lakes are used for various purposes such as hydroelectric power generation, irrigation, and recreation, and their creation has had both positive and negative impacts on the environment and local communities."}

